; The profiling of a benchmark, for a BlitzLLVM build with --profile (the runners use it with their --profile option): the GPU time of
; the passes of the last frame, read with ProfileValue after every Flip. It is not tied to the once-a-second report of ProfileFPS or
; BLITZLLVM_PROFILE_FPS, so every timed frame counts and a short run has numbers too. The GPU times come back a frame or two late, so
; the first frames read 0 and are left out. The runners copy it (or bench_profile_off.bi) next to the benchmark as bench_profile.bi.

Function BenchProfiling()
	Return 1
End Function

; One number of the last frame in milliseconds, by its key: "gpu scene", "gpu 2d", "gpu copy", "gpu present", "gpu frame", see ProfileValue.
Function BenchProfile#(key$)
	Return ProfileValue(key$)
End Function
